<section class="hero small">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
    <h1>Built to be repaired, not replaced.</h1>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap prose">
  <h2>Our story</h2>
  <p>We started in 2012 in a garage in Bergen with one tent design and a sewing machine. Today we're a team of 40, but the idea hasn't changed: make outdoor gear that lasts, and fix it when it doesn't.</p>
  <h2>Our numbers</h2>
  <div class="stats">
    <div><b>8,214</b><span>repairs in 2025</span></div>
    <div><b>92%</b><span>recycled fabrics</span></div>
    <div><b>3 min</b><span>average chat reply</span></div>
  </div>
  <h2>Our team</h2>
  <p>Our support team are all active hikers and climbers. When you chat with us, you're talking to someone who has slept in the gear they're recommending.</p>
  <ul class="team">
    <li><b>Mohsin Kabir</b> — Head of support</li>
    <li><b>Imran Hossain</b> — Gear expert</li>
    <li><b>Farhana Akter</b> — Returns &amp; warranty</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Sustainability</h2>
  <p>Every tent ships with spare pole sections and a patch kit. Worn-out gear can be returned to us for recycling, and you get store credit for it.</p>
</section>
